values('project-programme-portfolio-01','project-programme-portfolio',2,'1.5','An organisation coordinates a new appointment website, staff training and redesigned telephone processes to reduce missed appointments. Which description best fits that joint coordination?','[{"id":"a","text":"One work package within the website project."},{"id":"b","text":"Routine service operation only."},{"id":"c","text":"Programme management of related change and benefits."},{"id":"d","text":"Portfolio selection of unrelated investments only."}]'::jsonb,'c','Related initiatives and operational change are coordinated to produce a combined benefit, which is programme work. A work package is a smaller delivery unit. Portfolio management focuses on investment alignment and balance; routine operations alone do not describe the coordinated change.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-programme-portfolio-02','project-programme-portfolio',2,'1.5','There is insufficient specialist capacity to fund every proposed change initiative. Which decision most clearly belongs at portfolio level?','[{"id":"a","text":"Choose and balance investments against strategy and available capacity."},{"id":"b","text":"Assign tomorrow’s testing tasks inside one project."},{"id":"c","text":"Accept an individual deliverable against its specification."},{"id":"d","text":"Resolve a spelling error in a project report."}]'::jsonb,'a','Portfolio management concerns which investments should proceed and how the overall mix supports strategy and capacity. The other decisions concern delivery or administration within individual projects.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-programme-portfolio-03','project-programme-portfolio',2,'1.4','Why does an organisation use project management rather than simply letting each specialist complete their own tasks independently?','[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure that the project manager performs every technical task."},{"id":"b","text":"To replace all specialist judgement with a fixed schedule."},{"id":"c","text":"To remove the need to make trade-offs."},{"id":"d","text":"To coordinate work and control delivery towards agreed objectives."}]'::jsonb,'d','Project management integrates specialist contributions and handles constraints, dependencies and uncertainty. Specialists still provide expertise, and trade-offs still need decisions. A schedule supports this work but does not replace it.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-programme-portfolio-04','project-programme-portfolio',2,'1.3','Which activity best illustrates project management rather than only specialist delivery?','[{"id":"a","text":"A technician configures a single scanner."},{"id":"b","text":"The manager integrates scope, schedule, resources and risk decisions towards the agreed change."},{"id":"c","text":"An operator sells the same tickets each day after handover."},{"id":"d","text":"A designer selects a colour without reference to any agreed objective."}]'::jsonb,'b','Project management coordinates and controls contributions towards objectives. Configuring a component is specialist work, and routine ticket sales are operations. An isolated preference without an objective does not describe integrated management.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-programme-portfolio-05','project-programme-portfolio',2,'1.5','Why might portfolio leaders decide not to start a well-defined project that has a credible business case?','[{"id":"a","text":"A credible case guarantees priority over every other investment."},{"id":"b","text":"Portfolio management is limited to checking individual task durations."},{"id":"c","text":"Another mix of investments better fits strategy, risk appetite and available capacity."},{"id":"d","text":"A project can only belong to a portfolio if it shares a supplier with every other component."}]'::jsonb,'c','A sound individual case does not settle the organisation-wide priority decision. Portfolio leaders balance the overall investment mix and constraints. Common suppliers and individual task durations do not define portfolio selection.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
