values('business-case-05','business-case',2,'4.4','Why should a business case compare the preferred proposal with doing nothing or doing the minimum?','[{"id":"a","text":"To prove that doing nothing is always the best option."},{"id":"b","text":"To eliminate all assumptions about costs and benefits."},{"id":"c","text":"To make the incremental costs, benefits and risks of investment visible."},{"id":"d","text":"To avoid involving the sponsor in the investment decision."}]'::jsonb,'c','A baseline alternative helps decision-makers judge what changes because of the proposed investment. It does not predetermine the answer, remove uncertainty or replace the sponsor’s decision-making responsibility.')
