values('project-life-cycles-02','project-life-cycles',2,'2.4','Why would an extended life-cycle view continue beyond handover of equipment?','[{"id":"a","text":"To prevent operational owners taking responsibility."},{"id":"b","text":"To keep every temporary project team member employed indefinitely."},{"id":"c","text":"To avoid defining acceptance criteria."},{"id":"d","text":"To consider adoption, outcomes and benefits after outputs enter use."}]'::jsonb,'d','Value may arise after handover and needs operational ownership and review. An extended view does not remove acceptance criteria or imply that the temporary delivery team continues forever.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-life-cycles-03','project-life-cycles',2,'2.2','Which feature best characterises iterative delivery?','[{"id":"a","text":"No initial direction and no decisions about constraints."},{"id":"b","text":"Repeated development and review that use feedback to refine the work."},{"id":"c","text":"A ban on engaging users until everything is finished."},{"id":"d","text":"A guarantee that no requirement will change."}]'::jsonb,'b','Iteration creates opportunities to learn and refine through repeated cycles. It still needs direction, constraints and governance. Delaying all feedback or assuming fixed detailed requirements defeats that learning purpose.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-life-cycles-04','project-life-cycles',2,'2.1','In a typical linear life cycle, which sequence places the main phases in a sensible order?','[{"id":"a","text":"Concept, definition, deployment, transition."},{"id":"b","text":"Transition, deployment, definition, concept."},{"id":"c","text":"Deployment, transition, concept, definition."},{"id":"d","text":"Definition, benefits review, concept, initial investigation."}]'::jsonb,'a','The idea and viability are explored before detailed definition, followed by carrying out the work and transition into use. Organisations may use different phase labels, but reversing those purposes is not a credible linear sequence.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-life-cycles-05','project-life-cycles',2,'2.2','An iterative team reviews working outputs with users at the end of each cycle. What should happen to useful feedback?','[{"id":"a","text":"Discard it because planning happened once at the beginning."},{"id":"b","text":"Implement every suggestion immediately without considering priorities or constraints."},{"id":"c","text":"Treat it as proof that governance is unnecessary."},{"id":"d","text":"Use it to refine understanding and prioritise later work within agreed controls."}]'::jsonb,'d','Iteration creates opportunities to learn and adapt. Feedback should inform choices within the project’s constraints and authority, rather than being ignored or automatically implemented without assessment.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-management-plan-01','project-management-plan',2,'4.1','A manager replaces the approved deployment baseline with the latest forecast without authorisation. What is the main problem?','[{"id":"a","text":"Forecasts must never be updated."},{"id":"b","text":"The project can no longer hold team meetings."},{"id":"c","text":"The reference for assessing variance and controlling change has been lost."},{"id":"d","text":"The business case automatically becomes a work breakdown structure."}]'::jsonb,'c','A baseline is an authorised control reference, while a forecast is the current expectation. Forecasts should be updated honestly; baseline changes need the agreed authority. Neither meeting arrangements nor document renaming addresses the control problem.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-management-plan-02','project-management-plan',2,'4.3','Which group should contribute to or be considered when developing a project management plan?','[{"id":"a","text":"Relevant sponsor, delivery, user, operational and supplier stakeholders."},{"id":"b","text":"Only the person who formats the schedule."},{"id":"c","text":"Only people who have no involvement in acceptance."},{"id":"d","text":"Every external person must approve every plan detail."}]'::jsonb,'a','The plan depends on stakeholder assumptions, constraints, responsibilities and acceptance needs. Involvement should be relevant and proportionate; it does not mean everyone approves everything or that planning is only document formatting.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-management-plan-03','project-management-plan',2,'4.10','What is the best reason to agree measurable success criteria near the start?','[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure success can never be questioned."},{"id":"b","text":"To make risk management unnecessary."},{"id":"c","text":"To guarantee every stakeholder values exactly the same thing."},{"id":"d","text":"To align expectations and provide evidence for delivery decisions and acceptance."}]'::jsonb,'d','Success criteria clarify how results will be judged and support decisions and acceptance. They do not guarantee success, remove uncertainty or eliminate legitimate differences between stakeholders.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-management-plan-04','project-management-plan',2,'4.2','How can a deployment baseline differ between linear and iterative delivery?','[{"id":"a","text":"An iterative project cannot have any agreed budget or delivery constraints."},{"id":"b","text":"Linear work may baseline detailed scope early; iterative work may refine near-term detail within agreed overall constraints."},{"id":"c","text":"A linear baseline must be rewritten silently whenever a forecast changes."},{"id":"d","text":"Iterative work guarantees that every requirement is completely defined before the first cycle."}]'::jsonb,'b','The level and timing of detail can differ while authorised control references still exist. Iteration does not mean no control, and linear delivery does not justify unapproved changes to the baseline.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('project-management-plan-05','project-management-plan',2,'4.10','At handover, what is a particularly useful role for previously agreed success criteria?','[{"id":"a","text":"Replace all evidence with the manager’s personal confidence."},{"id":"b","text":"Make future benefit measurement impossible."},{"id":"c","text":"Provide a shared basis for judging acceptance and outstanding conditions."},{"id":"d","text":"Guarantee that operational adoption has already delivered every long-term benefit."}]'::jsonb,'c','Success criteria help the relevant parties judge whether conditions for acceptance have been met. They require evidence and do not automatically demonstrate benefits that arise only after sustained use.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
