values('scope-management-01','scope-management',2,'5.3','Which pairing correctly distinguishes a PBS from a WBS?','[{"id":"a","text":"PBS is the schedule; WBS is the contract register."},{"id":"b","text":"PBS shows required products; WBS breaks down the work to produce them."},{"id":"c","text":"PBS lists only people; WBS lists only invoice numbers."},{"id":"d","text":"PBS and WBS are both automatically ordered by time."}]'::jsonb,'b','A PBS describes the product hierarchy and a WBS the work hierarchy. Neither is automatically a schedule. Organisational and cost views are separate breakdowns, not substitutes for these two purposes.')
