values('resource-scheduling-01','resource-scheduling',2,'6.2','A takes 2 days. B takes 3 days after A. C takes 4 days after A. D takes 2 days after both B and C. With sufficient resources, what is the earliest finish?','[{"id":"a","text":"8 days, determined by A–C–D."},{"id":"b","text":"7 days, determined by A–B–D."},{"id":"c","text":"11 days because B and C must always be sequential."},{"id":"d","text":"4 days because C is the longest individual activity."}]'::jsonb,'a','The parallel paths take 7 and 8 days; the longer dependency chain determines completion. B and C need not be sequential when resources permit parallel working. The longest single activity is not the same as the critical path.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('resource-scheduling-02','resource-scheduling',2,'6.5','An activity is moved only within available float to reduce a resource peak while retaining the finish date. What is this?','[{"id":"a","text":"Benefits realisation."},{"id":"b","text":"Automatic scope acceptance."},{"id":"c","text":"A procurement strategy."},{"id":"d","text":"Resource smoothing."}]'::jsonb,'d','Smoothing uses available flexibility while preserving the finish date. Levelling addresses resource limits and may extend completion. Benefits, scope acceptance and procurement concern other management decisions.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('resource-scheduling-03','resource-scheduling',2,'6.6','Which description best fits a procurement strategy?','[{"id":"a","text":"The order in which a report’s pages are printed."},{"id":"b","text":"An approach to obtaining required goods/services, including sourcing, contracting and risk/timing choices."},{"id":"c","text":"A guarantee to select the lowest price in every case."},{"id":"d","text":"A list of completed lesson titles."}]'::jsonb,'b','Procurement strategy addresses how the required supply will be obtained and managed. Price is one consideration, alongside capability, contracts, timing and risk. A printing sequence or unrelated list is not a sourcing approach.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('resource-scheduling-04','resource-scheduling',2,'6.3','What distinguishes a milestone from a normal schedule activity?','[{"id":"a","text":"It marks a significant event or decision and has zero duration."},{"id":"b","text":"It is always the longest task in the project."},{"id":"c","text":"It contains every resource assignment."},{"id":"d","text":"It automatically replaces a decision gate’s evidence."}]'::jsonb,'a','A milestone marks an event, not a duration of work. Work leading to it still needs activities, resources and evidence; the marker itself does not perform or authorise that work.')
