values('leadership-and-teamwork-01','leadership-and-teamwork',2,'10.4','A new team needs orientation and clearer roles, and members are beginning to disagree about ways of working. How can Tuckman’s model help?','[{"id":"a","text":"Prove that the team will improve without leadership action."},{"id":"b","text":"Suggest forming/storming needs to explore, while the manager listens and adapts support."},{"id":"c","text":"Require the manager to dismiss everyone who disagrees."},{"id":"d","text":"Replace observation with a permanent label for each person."}]'::jsonb,'b','The model helps diagnose possible team needs, not predict inevitable progress or label individuals. Constructive disagreement needs appropriate support; ignoring it or treating all disagreement as misconduct is not justified by the model.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('leadership-and-teamwork-02','leadership-and-teamwork',2,'10.4','A team has strong ideas but little attention to organising implementation and checking detail. What is a useful Belbin-based response?','[{"id":"a","text":"Recruit exactly nine people, regardless of project needs."},{"id":"b","text":"Assign each person a permanent job title based only on a label."},{"id":"c","text":"Discuss missing contributions and how existing members or support could provide them."},{"id":"d","text":"Assume only the sponsor can contribute practical organisation."}]'::jsonb,'c','Belbin can prompt discussion of complementary contributions. Roles are not fixed job titles and one person can contribute in several ways. Team composition should address actual needs, not a compulsory headcount.')
on conflict(id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,syllabus_ref=excluded.syllabus_ref,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
insert into apm_private.checkpoint_questions as current (id,lesson_id,content_version,syllabus_ref,stem,choices,correct_option_id,explanation)
values('leadership-and-teamwork-03','leadership-and-teamwork',2,'10.2','Which manager behaviour is most likely to support team performance?','[{"id":"a","text":"Clarify shared goals, invite early concerns and remove obstacles."},{"id":"b","text":"Reward silence about emerging problems."},{"id":"c","text":"Assume formal authority guarantees commitment."},{"id":"d","text":"Use the same support approach regardless of experience or circumstances."}]'::jsonb,'a','Clear direction, constructive feedback and practical support help people contribute. Suppressing concerns or relying solely on authority can hide problems. Leadership should respond to the situation and team needs.')
